        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: багажник",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "багажник (bagázhnik) — \"a boot (of a car); a roof rack\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Чемоданы лежат в багажнике. Chemodány lezhát v bagázhnike. The suitcases are in the boot."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Built on багаж — luggage. In American English, the trunk."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "багажник (bagázhnik) is built on багаж 'luggage' with the ending -ник, the place for it. Багаж was borrowed from French bagage 'baggage, luggage' (EtymDB); EtymDB does not list багажник (bagázhnik) itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
