          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "дворник (dvórnik) — \"a windscreen wiper; a caretaker, a street sweeper\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Шёл дождь, и дворники работали всю дорогу. Shyol dozhd, i dvórniki rabótali vsyu dorógu. It was raining, and the wipers worked all the way."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first meaning is a person who sweeps a yard; the wipers sweep the glass."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "дворник (dvórnik) is built on двор 'a yard' (EtymDB), which is inherited from Proto-Slavic dvorŭ 'a court'. EtymDB glosses дворник (dvórnik) as the one who keeps the yard and the pavement; the wiper that sweeps the glass took the name later."
            }
          ]
        },
